id: intuit
name: Intuit
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: true
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
intuit: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Read an Opponent. They are Seen until the end of your next turn, and your Skill Checks
  and Saving Throws in Clashes against them gain 2 and 1(T).
text: >
  Intuit Maneuver [1/Round]: Following your gut, you predict your opponent’s next move.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: N/A
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Target an Opponent, that Opponent becomes ‘Seen’ until the end of your next
  turn. Increase the Dice Score of your Skill Checks and Saving Throws in Clashes against
  a Seen Opponent by 2 and 1(T) respectively.

---

# The Analysis Maneuver's sibling: a mark on somebody else, a clock kept by you, and a
# bonus that is yours against them. Built the same way, and the file says where each half
# lives.
#
# No script. Both halves are about a pair - the mark goes on somebody else and the bonus is
# measured against them - and a passive writes Slots onto the character holding it.
#
# What it comes to:
#   - the target is marked Seen, a Condition with no effects of its own
#   - the clock sits on you: "until the end of YOUR next turn" is your turn, and a duration
#     one character keeps over another is what `on` is for
#   - that clock is also the record of who read whom
#   - the bonus is applied where a Clash builds the side that is rolling
#
# --- "Respectively", which is two numbers and two rolls -------------------------------------
#
# "Increase the Dice Score of your Skill Checks and Saving Throws in Clashes against a Seen
# Opponent by 2 and 1(T) respectively." Two different amounts for two different rolls, and
# the second is scaled where the first is flat - so they are two rows rather than one, and
# a Clash gets whichever of them it is made of.
#
# --- "In Clashes" is the whole of the scope ----------------------------------------------------
#
# Not every Skill Check and not every Saving Throw: only the ones made in a Clash, which is
# what the sentence says and is also the only place "against a Seen Opponent" has a meaning.
# A Skill Check rolled off the sheet is against nobody.
#
# So it is applied where a Clash assembles the side that is rolling, and the two categories
# that get it are the two the sentence names: a Skill Clash and a Clash of Saving Throws. A
# Might Clash is neither and gets nothing; a Grapple Check is a Combat Roll and gets nothing
# either - that is Analysis's half of the pair.
#
# --- The reading of "your Clashes against a Seen Opponent" ----------------------------------------
#
# Taken as: yours against the Opponent you read. The wider reading - that any Seen Opponent
# is fair game for anybody who has this Maneuver - is the same one the Analysis file weighs
# and rejects, for the same reason: the narrow one cannot be wrong by accident, and if the
# wider one is meant the change is the one line that asks whose clock it is.
#
# --- How it is gained ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A Special Maneuver, and what opens it has not been read yet. Intuition is the obvious
# guess, which is worth nothing - the Dirty Trick is a Clash made with Bluff and Bluff opens
# the Feint instead.
